No, there's no way in an ASA to define a group as not-Something. But:

    10 deny ip &lt;source&gt; &lt;RCF1918&gt;
    20 permit ip &lt;source&gt; any

and

    10 permit ip &lt;source&gt; &lt;not-RFC1918&gt;

are functionally identical. You would need to define the RFC1918 and not-RFC1918 objects yourself.
